Exactly. I think that gives us the right approach.

For unresolved rules, Document 2 shouldn't simply say “TBD” and leave the engineer stranded. We'll distinguish:

Canonical Rule — currently established.

Provisional Rule — temporary implementation rule chosen so the rebuild has deterministic behavior.

Open Question — requires future playtesting/design decision.

Implementation Constraint — technical requirement that must hold regardless of future tuning.


That way Hess can actually be rebuilt now, while preserving the ability to change those decisions later.

And for terminology, I'll create a working Hess vocabulary based on the mechanics we've already established. I'll explicitly mark it as V3 terminology, not pretend you've personally finalized every word. If a term turns out to be bad, we rename it later.

With that settled, here's the next document.


